                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.19857/2611.19857v1/pandwm_architecture.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:PanDWM overview.\n(a) Panoramic history is split into overlapping halves and encoded by a VAE. Conditioned on layouts, text and ray maps, a causal diffusion transformer predicts 16 frames from 3 history frames in four steps; its final 3 frames seed the next window.\n(b) A feed-forward decoder lifts frame latents into pixel-aligned Gaussians along calibrated source-camera rays, at ranges relabelled with Depth Anything 3. Static geometry from neighbouring frames supports 4D completion.\nPanoramas are displayed as cylindrical bands; ellipsoids are enlarged for display.",
                "position": 433
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "header": "3Method",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.19857/2611.19857v1/pandwm_geometry.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Gaussian geometry and completion.\n(a) Panoramic pixels retain their calibrated source-camera origins.\n(b) Range and offset locate Gaussians relative to these rays (Eq.3); both halves’ predictions are retained in the overlap.\n(c) Ego-motion-aligned neighbouring static Gaussians fill uncovered pixels, while dynamic content comes from the current frame.",
                "position": 571
            }
        ]
